================================================================================
2. Private vs. public hosting
================================================================================

A server is PRIVATE only if ALL of the following are true:
  a) Access is restricted by at least one technical control:
       - a VPN or private network not reachable from the internet, OR
       - an authentication layer in front of the app (e.g. reverse proxy
         auth, SSO), OR
       - a firewall / WAF / IP allowlist limited to specific addresses;
  b) No more than 10 people can access it;
  c) Every person with access is known to you personally; and
  d) It is not advertised, listed, or shared publicly (including links).

Any server that does not meet ALL of the above is PUBLIC.

Please respect the wishes of the original creator.

